omplex-mabxl-where-a-b-jee-main-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-3q2tan4headpwvou","question":{"en":{"comprehension":null,"direction":null,"content":"<p>The metal atom present in the complex MABXL (where A, B, X and L are unidentate ligands and <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.075ex\" height=\"1.545ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 917 683\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4D\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> is metal) involves <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.137ex\" height=\"2.324ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -833.2 1386.6 1027.2\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"73\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-73\"></use><use data-c=\"70\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-70\" transform=\"translate(394,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(983,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> hybridization. The number of geometrical isomers exhibited by the complex is :</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"0"},{"identifier":"B","content":"2"},{"identifier":"C","content":"3"},{"identifier":"D","content":"4"}],"correct_options":["A"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p>To determine the number of geometrical isomers for the given complex <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"8.484ex\" height=\"1.62ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -716 3750 716\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4D\"></use><use data-c=\"41\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-41\" transform=\"translate(917,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"42\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-42\" transform=\"translate(1667,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"58\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-58\" transform=\"translate(2375,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"4C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4C\" transform=\"translate(3125,0)\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, where <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.075ex\" height=\"1.545ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 917 683\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4D\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> is a metal and <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.697ex\" height=\"1.62ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -716 750 716\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"41\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-41\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.602ex\" height=\"1.545ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 708 683\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"42\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-42\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.697ex\" height=\"1.545ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 750 683\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"58\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-58\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, and <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.414ex\" height=\"1.545ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 625 683\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4C\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> are unidentate ligands, we need to consider the geometry implied by the <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.137ex\" height=\"2.324ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -833.2 1386.6 1027.2\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"73\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-73\"></use><use data-c=\"70\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-70\" transform=\"translate(394,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(983,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> hybridization of the metal. The <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.137ex\" height=\"2.324ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -833.2 1386.6 1027.2\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"73\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-73\"></use><use data-c=\"70\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-70\" transform=\"translate(394,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(983,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> hybridization suggests a tetrahedral geometry for the metal complex.</p>\n\n<p>In a tetrahedral complex, geometrical isomerism does not arise. This is because geometrical isomerism (also known as cis-trans isomerism) typically occurs in square planar or octahedral complexes where ligands can be positioned differently around the central metal atom to give distinct isomers. In a tetrahedral complex, every position is equivalent due to the symmetric arrangement of the ligands around the metal center, making it impossible to distinguish between different sides of the molecule as you would with a square planar or octahedral complex.</p>\n\n<p>Given that the complex follows tetrahedral geometry because of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.137ex\" height=\"2.324ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -833.2 1386.6 1027.2\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"73\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-73\"></use><use data-c=\"70\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-70\" transform=\"translate(394,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(983,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> hybridization and that tetrahedral complexes do not exhibit geometrical isomerism, the number of geometrical isomers exhibited by the complex is:</p>\n\n<p>Option A: 0</p>\n\n<p>This is because in a tetrahedral arrangement of ligands around a metal center, no geometrical isomers can be formed due to the lack of cis or trans arrangements possible within such a symmetric geometry.</p>"},"hi":{"comprehension":null,"direction":null,"content":"<p>कॉम्प्लेक्स MABXL (जहाँ A, B, X और L चतुर्दिकीय लिगैंड्स हैं और <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.075ex\" height=\"1.545ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 917 683\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4D\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> धातु है) में सम्मिलित धातु परमाणु <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.137ex\" height=\"2.324ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -833.2 1386.6 1027.2\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"73\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-73\"></use><use data-c=\"70\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-70\" transform=\"translate(394,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(983,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> हाइब्रिडाइजेशन शामिल करता है। इस कॉम्प्लेक्स द्वारा प्रदर्शित ज्यामितीय आइसोमर्स की संख्या है:</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"0"},{"identifier":"B","content":"2"},{"identifier":"C","content":"3"},{"identifier":"D","content":"4"}],"correct_options":["A"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p>दिए गए संकुल <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.452ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"17.765ex\" height=\"2.149ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -750 7852 950\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtext\" style=\"font-family: Roboto,'Tiro Devanagari Hindi','Tiro Bangla',sans-serif;\"><text data-variant=\"-explicitFont\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\" font-size=\"884px\"> </text