erflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.697ex\" height=\"1.62ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -716 750 716\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"41\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-41\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.602ex\" height=\"1.545ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 708 683\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"42\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-42\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.697ex\" height=\"1.545ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 750 683\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"58\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-58\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, और <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.414ex\" height=\"1.545ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 625 683\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4C\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> एकदंतुर लिगैंड हैं, हमें धातु के <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.137ex\" height=\"2.324ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -833.2 1386.6 1027.2\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"73\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-73\"></use><use data-c=\"70\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-70\" transform=\"translate(394,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(983,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> संकरण द्वारा निहित ज्यामिति पर विचार करने की आवश्यकता है। <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.137ex\" height=\"2.324ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -833.2 1386.6 1027.2\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"73\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-73\"></use><use data-c=\"70\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-70\" transform=\"translate(394,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(983,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> संकरण धातु संकुल के लिए एक चतुष्फलकीय ज्यामिति का सुझाव देता है।</p><p>एक चतुष्फलकीय संकुल में, ज्यामितीय समावयवता उत्पन्न नहीं होती है। ऐसा इसलिए है क्योंकि ज्यामितीय समावयवता (जिसे सिस-ट्रांस समावयवता के रूप में भी जाना जाता है) आमतौर पर वर्ग समतलीय या अष्टफलकीय संकुलों में होती है जहाँ लिगैंड केंद्रीय धातु परमाणु के चारों ओर भिन्न रूप से स्थित हो सकते हैं और विशिष्ट समावयव बना सकते हैं। एक चतुष्फलकीय संकुल में, धातु केंद्र के चारों ओर लिगैंडों की सममित व्यवस्था के कारण प्रत्येक स्थिति समतुल्य होती है, जिससे अणु के विभिन्न पक्षों के बीच अंतर करना असंभव हो जाता है जैसा कि आप एक वर्ग समतलीय या अष्टफलकीय संकुल के साथ करेंगे।</p><p>यह देखते हुए कि संकुल <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.137ex\" height=\"2.324ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -833.2 1386.6 1027.2\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"73\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-73\"></use><use data-c=\"70\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-70\" transform=\"translate(394,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(983,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> संकरण के कारण चतुष्फलकीय ज्यामिति का पालन करता है और चतुष्फलकीय संकुल ज्यामितीय समावयवता प्रदर्शित नहीं करते हैं, संकुल द्वारा प्रदर्शित ज्यामितीय समावयवों की संख्या है:</p><p>विकल्प A: 0</p><p>ऐसा इसलिए है क्योंकि धातु केंद्र के चारों ओर लिगैंडों की चतुष्फलकीय व्यवस्था में, इस तरह की सममित ज्यामिति के भीतर संभव सिस या ट्रांस व्यवस्थाओं की कमी के कारण कोई ज्यामितीय समावयव नहीं बन सकते हैं।</p>"}},"subject":"chemistry","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":120000,"topic":"isomerism-of-coordination-compounds","type":"mcq","year":2024,"isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"tags":[],"yearKey":"jee-main-2024-online-5th-april-evening-shift","active":true,"options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"0"},{"identifier":"B","content":"2"},{"identifier":"C","content":"3"},{"identifier":"D","content":"4"}],"correct_options":["A"],"explanation":"<p>To determine the number of geometrical isomers for the given complex <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"8.484ex\" height=\"1.62ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -716 3750 716\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4D\"></use><use data-c=\"41\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-41\" transform=\"translate(917,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"42\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-42\" transform=\"translate(1667,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"58\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-58\" transform=\"translate(2375,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"4C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4C\" transform=\"translate(3125,0)\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, where <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.075ex\" height=\"1.545ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 917 683\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4D\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> is a metal and <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.697ex\" height=\"1.62ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -716 750 716\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"41\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-41\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.602ex\" height=\"1.545ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 708 683\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"42\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-42\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.697ex\" height=\"1.545ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 750 683\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"58\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-58\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, and <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.414ex\" height=\"1.545ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 625 683\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4C\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> are unidentate ligands, we need to consider the geometry implied by the <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.137ex\" height=\"2.324ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -833.2 1386.6 1027.2\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"73\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-73\"></use><use data-c=\"70\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-70\" transform=\"translate(394,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(983,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> hybridization of the metal. The <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.137ex\" height=\"2.324ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -833.2 1386.6 1027.2\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"73\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-73\"></use><use data-c=\"70\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-70\" transform=\"translate(394,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(983,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> hybridization suggests a tetrahedral geometry for the metal complex.</p>\n\n<p>In a tetrahedral complex, geometrical isomerism does not arise. This is because geometrical isomerism (also known as cis-trans isomerism) typically occurs in square planar or octahedral complexes where ligands can be positioned differently around the central metal atom to give distinct isomers. In a tetrahedral complex, every position is equivalent due to the symmetric arrangement of the ligands around the metal center, making it impossible to distinguish between different sides of the molecule as you would with a square planar or octahedral complex.</p>\n\n<p>Given that the complex follows tetrahedral geometry because of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.137ex\" height=\"2.324ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -833.2 1386.6 1027.2\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"73\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-73\"></use><use data-c=\"70\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-70\" transform=\"translate(394,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(983,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> hybridization and that tetrahedral complexes do not exhibit geometrical isomerism, the number of geometrical isomers exhibited by the complex is:</p>\n\n<p>Option A: 0</p>\n\n<p>This is because in a tetrahedral arrangement of ligands around a metal center, no geometrical isomers can be formed due to the lack of cis or trans arrangements possible within such a symmetric geometry.</p>"}]}